    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_secondary_differential_certifier",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 secondary gap has an equivalent differential certifier",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "After the generic primary double gap, write B=sum_(n=0)^(2H-3) a_nz^n, b=a_(2H-3), c=a_(2H), and kappa=E_4b/c. The primary residual is exactly E'B+4EB'=-8Hc z^(2H-1)+8(H-1)E_4b z^(2H). In official characteristic, the secondary square LT=cC^2 mod z^H is equivalent to z^H dividing zE'C^2+4HEC^2+4zECC'-(4H-4(H-1)kappa z)B for one C(0)=1 of degree at most H-3. This removes the high coefficient window but does not force parity or impose torsion.",
